{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966803,"nonce":"OpyMM8zvtWORKilLYWxMAXkiY1I=","title":"Content built inside a Stateful callback cannot rely on inherited CSS: a bound cn.Badge","message":"**Symptom.** `cn.Badge(label = \u003csignal\u003e)` renders its text in the default\ncolour instead of the variant's. It corrects itself after interacting with\nsomething unrelated (a button elsewhere), which makes it look like a repaint\nbug. Static badges are always right.\n\n**Rule.** A widget's own CSS class colours its text by INHERITANCE, and that\nonly reaches content the stylesheet pass has walked. Content created by a\n`Stateful` callback is rebuilt after that pass, so it starts with whatever it\nwas built with and only picks up inherited values when some later event\ntriggers another pass. **Anything rebuilt inside a stateful must set its own\nvisual props.** `cn::Button` already did this -- it reads the CSS-resolved\n`text_color` off its config inside `on_state` -- which is why Button was fine\nand Badge was not.\n\n**Fix (f3189246).** `Badge::reactive_label` reads the variant's theme token in\nRust and sets `.color(fg)` on the rebuilt label. `label_color_token` mirrors\n`.cn-badge--{style}-{variant} { color }` and must be kept in step with it.\nTrade-off, accepted: a CSS override of that class no longer reaches a BOUND\nlabel (static labels still follow it). The deeper alternative is re-running\nthe class pass over rebuilt subtrees.\n\nAlso landed on the way (219486bc): keep the CLASS on a stable node outside the\nstateful and rebuild only the text inside. Necessary but not sufficient -- it\nfixes the ancestor chain, not the timing.\n\n**Diagnosing this class of bug.** `RenderTree::resolved_text_color(node)` was\nadded for it: \"the label is the wrong colour\" is otherwise only observable on\nscreen. Compare a bound widget against a static one node by node.\n`crates/blinc_cn/tests/badge_label_color.rs` does exactly that.\n\nTwo harness traps, both cost time:\n- `var(--text-secondary)` resolves at PARSE time against `ThemeState`, from the\n  app's stylesheet bundle. A unit test that parses CN_STYLES alone gets NO\n  colour at all, on static and bound alike, so it cannot tell them apart. Use a\n  literal colour to isolate structure from var resolution.\n- The user's report may predate the rebuild. Three of my \"it didn't work\"\n  rounds here were against a stale binary; say explicitly when a fix needs a\n  fresh build.\n\nSee gotcha class styles dropped on subtree rebuild,\nfeedback layout widgets theme tokens, project cn reactive prop migration.","files":null}]}